: "00ace89e2144512bae147f60ea1139297c193080"}], "patch": "patches/4ee410a0791abff8bff157989e8494941b7c507a-1/20260925T173327Z-1fd0d001.patch", "provenance": "verbatim", "runs": {}, "test_sources": [{"commit": "4ee410a0791abff8bff157989e8494941b7c507a", "paths": ["core/translate/collate.rs"]}], "tests": ["translate::collate::tests::test_resolve_comparison_collseq_uplus_and_parens_keep_column_collation"]}, "shard": "turso", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Merge 'optimizer: integrate hash joins better into cost model and fix hash-join associated bugs' from Jussi Saurio", "summary": "Comparison collation resolution ignored a left column's implicit BINARY collation, allowing a right NOCASE column to win and incorrectly match differently cased strings. The fix recognizes column operands through unary +, parentheses, and CAST, includes their default BINARY collation, and preserves explicit COLLATE precedence. The selected unit test was added by this fix and expects BINARY for a wrapped left column compared with a NOCASE right column. Reversing the selected implementation region should return NoCase instead; no tests were run.", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T17:33:43.866204+00:00"}
